  "description": "GIVPIO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C163 H118 Lu7 N27 O34 S6,2.5(C4 H8 O1),2.5(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu5 (Lu) has 6 O neighbors; Lu6 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu7 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu7A (Lu) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.069-3.827 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 21.92-122.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C163H118Lu7N27O34S6·2.5(C4H8O)·2.5(CH4O)·2(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
